From: Gleb Pesin <dormancygrace@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] bl2: read fip.bin directly instead of through the ROM loader

The ROM loader reads the FIP at about 9 MB/s even with the bus at 4 bits
and 50 MHz (0004), and prints a line per load. BL2 now finds fip.bin
itself, by name in the root directory of the first partition's FAT16 or
FAT32 file system as the ROM does, lists the runs of sectors it is
stored in (up to 16), and reads each part with one CMD18 per run
(CMD17 for one block): by SDMA into DRAM (OpenSBI, U-Boot: ~23 MB/s),
by PIO into BL2's SRAM (the parameter blocks; PIO tops out at ~8 MB/s,
and an SDMA transfer into SRAM reported completion before all its data
was there). The reader is used only when the first sector found is the
PARAM1 the ROM booted this BL2 with. Every load keeps its CRC check.

The SDHCI runs in version 4 mode (HOST_CONTROL2 bit 12, as the ROM left
it): the SDMA address goes into ADMA_SA, the block count into the 32-bit
register at 0x00, and the 16-bit count stays 0, as cv_emmc.c does.

Retries: on an SD boot the ROM reports one try per load, so a failed
load went straight to p_rom_api_flash_init() (the ROM gives up on SD for
eMMC) and the retry at the ROM's own bus settings 0004 provides was
never reached. An SD boot now tries each round three times: fip.bin
read directly, then the ROM loader, then the ROM loader at the ROM's
bus settings. The ROM's retry number (a backup copy on flash) is 0.
---
